  "name": null,
  "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}\\frac{2f(x)}{(1+4x)^{3}}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}\\frac{2f(x)}{(1+4x)^{3}}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "In part 1, we found that \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}f(x)=5.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}\\frac{2f(x)}{(1+4x)^{3}} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}(2f(x))}{{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}(1+4x)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, \n\n- applying the constant multiple rule in the numerator, and\n\n- the root rule, followed by the sum rule in the denominator,\n\nwe obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}(2f(x))}{{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}(1+4x)^{3}} & =\\frac{2\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}f(x)}{{({lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}(1+4x))}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}f(x)}{{(1+{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\pi /4}(4x))}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 5}{{(1+4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{(1+\\pi )^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
